00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.850 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to the panel channel  hosted by Z list comic youtubers ander  Mandela  I'm your host Xavier Mendez on this  inaugural episode I want to or I was s  tuba James look at this new Ben Riley  Scarlet Spider series by Peter David  this series is the triumphant return of  everyone's favorite hoodie wearing human  retcon Ben Riley spider-man's clone and  best bud who recently had a brief stint  as a supervillain where he argued that  he was morally righteous while laughing  maniacally subtlety what's that now Ben  is back with his own ongoing with the  intent to redeem his character written  by a veteran Spidey writer whom I want  to ask some very strange questions at a  convention after Ben Riley fails at  being a good villain he decides to flee  to Las Vegas so he can fail at being a  good hero in our first issue been  inexplicably has two voices in his head  representing the angels and devils that  make up his inner torment they never  show up again for some reason he also  runs around shooting people talking like  Deadpool lying stealing manipulating the  mother of a terminally ill child for  cash and taking advantage of the  mentally ill for companionship it's  pretty obvious that the intention at the  start of this book was for him to be  some kind of new character with Ben  Riley's name but I feel like the  backlash from fans was so heavy that  Peter David took a hard turn to write  him more like the character everyone  remembers or at least try to so after a  bunch of misadventures where he gets his  good costume back fights Spidey's other  clone Caine who is still alive for some  reason and then meets death you know the  lady that Deadpool and Thanos have a  love triangle with death tells Ben Riley  to stop acting like such a schmuck in  that he now operates on the Paragon  renegade system for his facial scarring  so he has to be a nice guy to look less  like a TJ Miller improvised line and we  get a story that feels a little bit more  classic  we've been bumping into the slingers a  bunch of random spider-man spin-offs  from the 90s  Kane takes more of a secondary character  position here it feels almost like a  team-up book with the two scarlet  spiders rather than a book solely about  Ben Riley then there's this current art  going where Kane is now doing all the  heavy lifting story wise while Ben sits  around doing nothing  so Kane hangs out with baseball players  and fights human hippo men no idea where  Peter David's going with this arc but I  guess I'll keep  reading alright so this book has shocked  me a bit by making it to as many as 14  issues the writing isn't bad but as you  can probably tell from the recap it's  all over the place ok well let's first  talk about the titular Scarlet Spider  Zhu Ben Riley's characterization has  gotten so muddled because there's so  many conflicting ideas of what he should  be like he doesn't currently feel like  how he did in the 90s he's just  something else one second he's acting a  lot like spider-man the next he's acting  really uncharacteristically violent and  cool and the next he's cracking some  pretty dark jokes he's bouncing around  between personalities so inconsistently  through the book that it's hard to root  for him it's one thing to have an  unpredictable main character but every  time you start to like him being one way  he pulls a 180 to be something else I  can't get attached to him as an edgy  antihero just like I can't get attached  to him as a good-hearted hero looking to  atone because he's both at the same time  and neither at the same time I have a  feeling Peter David had a really clear  vision of what he wanted Ben's  personality to be like in the series but  the backlash from fans over the first  few issues may have caused him to  backpedal in some scenes there's also  this weird lack of commitment towards  the new costume boy did they give up on  that one fast it just seems like this  series can't figure out what it wants to  be the fans and the writer are totally  at odds about what this book needs to  look like and the result ends up being  this weird hybrid of both ideas that's  so distorted it ends up leaving a bad  taste in your mouth  I'd say the saving grace of the  characters is Cain Cain is written to be  Walt himself here it's a little sad that  his own solo book ended on such rough  terms with all the side characters and  friends he made in Texas hating his guts  and losing theirs I feel like he was  really building a legacy for himself but  because of unsure sales in a poorly  thought-out crossover event he ended up  getting the shaft and his right back to  square one although I'm enjoying his  contributions to this series is the  second main character I was really  worried he'd be written out or killed  off in the first arc but he's stuck  around I'm pretty much enjoying his  subplot more than anything going on with  Ben Riley  the rest of the characters are just and  it's hard to like them or hate them they  just exist they're there so there's a  story there's Ben's boss Eva some lady  who runs a casino along with her  super-powered head of security she's  into some shady stuff and commits the  old non-law every now and then she also  has a terminally ill daughter that she's  basically forcing Ben to cure at  gunpoint which has made for some varied  scenes some good some kind of black the  villains and scenarios are also pretty  underwhelming thus far we do get to see  more of this section of the Marvel  Universe that's spider-man aftermath and  spin-offs but there's nothing super  compelling about the way it's told the  arc what the slingers kept taking a lot  of weird turns and felt like three  stories at once like okay this superhero  called the Hornet is trying to beat Ben  Riley whom he assumes as a villain  simple enough then he uses a magic  medallion to summon an elder God and  kill him because he's really sure he's a  bad guy weird but ok then he turns out  to be an obscure Wolverine villain  cyborg guy that came back from the dead  even though that contradicts what we saw  earlier you see what I mean this  sounding all over the place there were  times reading this stuff that I was  starting to wonder if it was all being  made up as he went along like one issue  gets written with no plan for what the  next one will be ok here's another  example Kane's facial scar is being  healed at the end of one issue but then  being scarred again right off the bat in  the next one with no explanation or  acknowledgement Peter David has written  some of the best comics out there and  he's probably one of my favorite Spidey  writers of all time but I just can't  help but wonder if his heart is into it  with this one as for the art well it's  all over the map too sometimes you get  really solid Mark Bagley art that's  always a joy to look at then sometimes  you get this other art that feels really  stiff and lifeless it feels like we'll  slimey's art is actually just a bunch of  tracings of only a handful of character  models because the faces are always so  similar and the body shape and  proportions have so little variation and  some of these poses look really awkward  like badly posed 3d models and not how  people move sometimes the art gets even  worse on a dialogue heavy issue I  noticed in this panel  new love interest has two left hands in  one right hand well the one hook hand  each also every episode the show will  not be posted on that other channel so  go subscribe to that the link is in the  description despite my misgivings about  it I do still find myself checking in on  this book every month to read more of it  Peter David's worst is still a cut above  the rest and I think that's attributed  to just how talented the guy really is  overall I think it has a chance to  stabilize and figure itself out as a  book but as we get further and further  into it with these issues still present  that seems more unlikely I do really  like the characters of Kane and Ben  Riley so I don't want this one to get  cancelled or awkwardly cut short before  it can shine here's hoping that with the  damnation crossover event things start  to take a turn for the better I really  liked a lot of the subsets spider-man  stuff in the Marvel Universe and while  they weren't exactly introduced in the  best way Ben Riley and Kane are two very  cool characters that I want to see stick  around for a long time seriously though  all future comic review videos will be  over there go subscribe to our Channel  what's wrong with you why haven't you  done it yet alright well see you next  month  [Music]  [Music]

